only eta-mu kanban count/list/find plus clojure -M:test. Retained the 2026-07-28 validate_rheos_board.py transcript in FT-OPS-001 as annotated history rather than deleting recorded evidence, because the run genuinely happened; annotated it as a removed tool citing ee10c65. Corrected FT-OPS-001 drift item 1, which falsely claimed the board contract had been corrected to the engine's real transitions, when f204d95 in fact removed the transition table entirely. Promoted the unenforced 2/1 WIP rule to its own explicit open-gap drift item instead of implying enforcement survives. Recorded FT-000A's acceptance basis as the human disposition comment 5099692071 and stated plainly that PR #3 carries no APPROVED review, rather than inventing an approval.", :drift "Six invariants died with the validator deleted in ee10c65 and are now enforced by nothing: (1) recursive scanning of nested cards below docs/kanban/<category>/, so a card at stories/player/foo.md is invisible to every check; (2) dependency-cycle rejection, so A -> B -> A now passes; (3) active-card readiness metadata (title/type/priority/phase/category/positive-points/owner, the five required sections, and a resolvable governing authority path), so a ready card with a nonexistent adr: path is accepted; (4) rejection of empty readiness sections, so five bare ## headings satisfy the gate; (5) the epic-state check restricting decomposed epics to breakdown/icebox/done/rejected; (6) the repository's stricter 2/1 in_progress/review WIP rule, whose rule text f204d95 also removed and which the promethean FSM contradicts at in_progress=50/review=40. Also unenforced: the trailing-newline requirement that eta-mu kanban frontmatter/comment writeback violates. NO upstream issue has been filed against open-hax/eta-mu or @eta-mu/rheos for any of these six; that filing remains outstanding and is not claimed as done. Rheos exposes no validate/lint verb in 1.1.1, so these checks currently have no expressible home in the sanctioned surface. eta-mu kanban --help and eta-mu kanban list --help both print only the generic banner, so the command surface was confirmed from CI and observed behaviour rather than from help output.", :note "Card prose only. No card status, uuid, owner, or other frontmatter field was changed on any card, and no board mutation was performed through eta-mu; all eta-mu use was read-only count/list/find. No audio device, native UI, waveform, FFmpeg, or publication API was exercised."}
