onstruction/preflight.clj and bb scripts/reconstruction/validate.clj -> usage, exit 2 with no arguments. git ls-files filtered for .cpcache, the eta-mu dot-directory, board.json, and .events -> empty.", :decisions "Reconciled by a real merge commit, never a rebase or force-push, so origin/design/media-workbench-v1 is an ancestor of PR #4 again and PR #3 history stays intact. Two conflicts, both resolved as judgment calls. AGENTS.md: took the base side wholesale for the Rheos board discipline and ecosystem sections, including the sole-authority prohibition, and took the base eta-mu kanban find verification line, while keeping this branch's Audio reconstruction section and the bb reconstruction preflight/validate lanes; the python3 scripts/validate_rheos_board.py line was dropped because the base banned it and the file no longer exists. receipts.edn: resolved as an append-only union rather than either side, with this branch's 26 rows in their existing order followed by the 4 rows unique to the base in their existing relative order; all 18 shared rows were byte-identical, so 26 + 4 = 30 with zero rows lost from either parent and zero duplicate lines. The deletion of scripts/validate_rheos_board.py was accepted, and .github/workflows/classifier-dsl.yml was taken as the base Rheos-installing version with permissions contents: read intact and exactly one workflow file tracked. Two truth repairs were made beyond the mechanical merge: the FT-003 epic still said four children and listed FT-003A through FT-003D, which the merge falsified by adding FT-003E as a fifth child, so the decomposition list, the acceptance criterion, and the verification block were extended and re-executed; and FT-OPS-003 called a 27-card count live evidence, so it was rewritten to rest on the absence of phantom prose rows rather than on a specific total, recording 27 as of the review and 28 on this branch.", :drift "No replacement validator, linter, or board checker was written, and no python3 scripts/validate_rheos_board.py CI step was reinstated; the six invariants that died with that script remain enforced by nothing and are still owned upstream in open-hax/eta-mu, with no upstream issue filed. git grep validate_rheos_board outside receipts.edn returns 3 hits, all in FT-OPS-001 and all byte-identical to the base, being one retained dated transcript plus two annotation lines that name the path only to state it was deleted and may not be restored; zero executable instructions remain. Dated 27-card transcripts in FT-OPS-001, FT-OPS-002, kanban-docs/README.md, and kanban-docs/BOARD-BREAKDOWN.md were deliberately left unedited because they are evidence of runs that really happened at 27 cards; only the one present-tense live-evidence claim was corrected. The FT-003 epic points field was left at 21 and not recalculated for FT-003E, because epic points are not a children sum in this corpus, as FT-000 shows with 13 against children summing to 17. No board mutation was performed: all eta-mu use was read-only count/list/find, and the frontmatter and comment write paths were avoided given their recorded frontmatter-rewrite corruption. The test count rose from the base 23 tests / 91 assertions to 41 tests / 184 assertions purely because the merge unions the classifier and reconstruction suites.", :note "FT-003E remains status incoming and was not implemented; FT-000B and FT-000D likewise untouched. The untracked 4.6G render tree was not imported, nothing was installed, no Python venv was rebuilt, and ~/Music was not written. Work performed in a throwaway worktree; the user's primary checkout at ~/spaces/fork_tales_v2 on design/classifier-dsl-v1 was never read from or written to."}
{:ts "2026-07-29T18:33:09Z", :kind :correction, :repo "https://github.com/octave-commons/fork_tales_v2", :origin "claude-code", :owner "claude-sonnet-5", :host "local-shell", :pi "eta-mu/receipt-river-v1", :dod "Address PR #3's five open, non-dispositioned review threads: select an FSM build gate that can pass in this Clojure repo, make FT-003's salvage editor consume FT-000D's architecture decision instead of choosing native UI/runtime downstream, add explicit child-dependency verification to the FT-001 and FT-003 epics, add Rheos evidence for the FT-001A-D player family to FT-OPS-002, and correct this ledger's own account of how card content is written.", :manifest "openhax.kanban.json, docs/kanban/epics/ft-003-salvage-and-arrangement.md, docs/kanban/stories/ft-003b-build-waveform-salvage-editor.md, docs/kanban/epics/ft-001-daily-driver-player.md, docs/kanban/chores/ft-ops-002-review-authority-statuses.md, receipts.edn", :refs "PR #3 review thread PRRT_kwDOTkaDCs6Uki5o; codex comment 3670149901 (openhax.kanban.json:3); CodeRabbit comments 3670162795 (ft-003:30), 3670162794/3670162792 (dependency+FT-001A-D evidence), 3670162796 (receipts.edn:22)", :tests "eta-mu --version -> 1.1.1. eta-mu kanban count -> 27 (unchanged: icebox 6, incoming 11, breakdown 4, ready 2, done 4). eta-mu kanban find resolved ft-003-...-non-destructively with updated dependency [\"ft-001-...-player\" \"ft-000d-...-topology\"]. eta-mu kanban find resolved all four FT-001A-D cards; all status incoming, each depending transitively on FT-000C and/or FT-000D. clojure -M:test -> Ran 23 tests containing 91 assertions, 0 failures, 0 errors, unaffected by these docs/config-only changes.", :decisions "openhax.kanban.json now sets fsm to {:extends \"promethean\" :buildGateCommands [\"clojure -M:test\"]}, the sanctioned per-project override resolve-fsm already supports, instead of the bare \"promethean\" string whose default build-gate ran pnpm build/lint/test against a repo with no pnpm project. FT-003's epic scope and acceptance criteria were reworded so the salvage editor implements FT-000D's selected UI/runtime and topology rather than hard-coding a native waveform editor choice; FT-003 and FT-003B both gained an explicit dependency on FT-000D. FT-001 and FT-003 epic verification sections now enumerate each child's expected `dependency` edge, so verification checks dependency edges through Rheos and not only resolution plus `epic` linkage. FT-OPS-002 gained real eta-mu kanban find output for FT-001A-D, since the existing verification result only evidenced FT-000A-D and FT-000C's own gating, not the player family's.", :drift "Correcting this ledger's own prior record rather than editing it: the entry at line 22 (:ts 2026-07-29T00:36:27Z) states 'Card prose only. No card status, uuid, owner, or other frontmatter field was changed on any card, and no board mutation was performed through eta-mu' as though that made the change compliant with Rheos board discipline. It does not. AGENTS.md's Rheos board discipline forbids a second Git/Markdown write protocol around board reads/writes/comments/transitions, and Rheos's own writeback implementation (rheos.backend.infra.task-writeback/write-task-status) exposes exactly one verb: rewriting a card's `status` frontmatter field plus a write-id. It has no verb for authoring body prose (Outcome/Scope/Acceptance criteria/Verification) or non-status frontmatter (dependency, owner, labels) in Rheos 1.1.1. Every prose and dependency edit made across this PR, including all edits listed in this entry's :manifest and every edit recorded in the entry at line 22, was therefore a direct Git/Markdown write outside Rheos CLI/API/MCP/UI -- the exact second write protocol AGENTS.md's board discipline names, not a neutral no-op merely because status/uuid/owner fields were untouched. This is recorded as a blocked capability rather than corrected in place: Rheos 1.1.1 has no sanctioned surface for card-content authoring, no upstream issue has been filed for it, and card corpus authoring in this repository has no compliant path until one exists. This entry does not delete or rewrite the line-22 entry -- ledger discipline forbids that -- it supersedes that entry's compliance framing while leaving its :tests/:decisions evidence intact as history.", :note "No card status, uuid, or eta-mu-mediated field was changed by this entry's edits either; the dependency arrays and prose above were still written by direct Markdown edit, same as every other card-authoring change in this PR, and are named as such rather than framed as board-compliant."}
{:ts "2026-07-29T18:50:20Z", :kind :correction, :repo "https://github.com/octave-commons/fork_tales_v2", :origin "claude-code", :owner "claude-sonnet-5", :host "local-shell", :pi "eta-mu/receipt-river-v1", :dod "Re-examine the claim made in the entry at :ts 2026-07-29T18:33:09Z that Rheos 1.1.1 has no verb for authoring non-status frontmatter, after being asked whether that reflected a real capability gap or just eta-mu's sparse --help making the capability undiscoverable.", :manifest "none (investigation only; no card or config file changed by this entry)", :refs "PR #3 review thread PRRT_kwDOTkaDCs6Uki5o; codex comment 3677119772 (ft-003b:17, 'Author board changes through Rheos'); prior receipts.edn entries at :ts 2026-07-29T00:36:27Z and 2026-07-29T18:33:09Z", :tests "Read source at /home/err/spaces/eta-mu/packages/rheos/src/rheos/backend/domain/task_edit.cljs: update-frontmatter! writes arbitrary frontmatter keys (any key, not just status) plus one ledger event per changed key; append-comment! appends a comment. Confirmed against the actually-installed package, not just the dev checkout: grep -o 'api/task/[^\"'\\'']*' on /home/err/.volta/tools/image/packages/eta-mu/lib/node_modules/eta-mu/node_modules/@eta-mu/rheos/dist/server.js (package.json version 0.1.0, bundled under the eta-mu package reporting version 1.1.1 on PATH) returned: GET api/task/:uuid/content (read-only, handle_get_task_content), PATCH api/task/:uuid/frontmatter (write, handle_update_frontmatter), POST api/task/:uuid/comment, POST api/task/:uuid/status, POST api/task/:uuid/open-editor. grep -o 'kanban_[a-z_]*' on the same dist/server.js returned only: kanban_add_comment, kanban_create_subtask, kanban_envelope, kanban_event, kanban_orchestrator, kanban_read_board, kanban_read_task, kanban_search_tasks, kanban_update_status -- no kanban_update_frontmatter tool. grep of dist/cli.cjs confirmed the complete CLI verb set: board, compose, move, status-update, add-comment, create-subtask, read-task, search-tasks, read-board, events, drift, serve -- no frontmatter/set/update verb. A live PATCH round-trip against a scratch project was attempted but not completed: the installed CLI's serve command ignores --port and a PORT env override and always binds 127.0.0.1:8791, which was already occupied by the user's own live Rheos server (PID 2889, connected to an open Firefox tab) -- correctly left untouched rather than killed or raced against.", :decisions "The claim in the 2026-07-29T18:33:09Z entry ('[Rheos] has no verb for authoring body prose ... or non-status frontmatter (dependency, owner, labels) in Rheos 1.1.1') is corrected, not edited: it was half right. Body prose (Outcome/Scope/Non-goals/Acceptance criteria/Verification) genuinely has no write path anywhere in Rheos 1.1.1 -- confirmed no CLI verb, no kanban_* tool, and the only content-adjacent HTTP route is GET-only. But frontmatter fields including `dependency` ARE writable, through `PATCH /api/task/:uuid/frontmatter`, backed by rheos.backend.domain.task-edit/update-frontmatter!, which existed the whole time. The real defect is not a missing Rheos capability but a discoverability gap: eta-mu kanban --help and every subcommand's --help print only the generic banner (already noted in the 2026-07-28T21:19:42Z entry), and this specific write route is wired into the HTTP server but never exposed as a CLI subcommand or an agent-tools/MCP tool, so nothing in this repository's documented workflow (or any agent following it) could have found or used it without reading the installed package's compiled source directly, as this entry did.", :drift "Two upstream gaps in open-hax/eta-mu / @eta-mu/rheos, distinct from the six already recorded in the 2026-07-29T00:36:27Z entry: (7) PATCH /api/task/:uuid/frontmatter, POST .../comment, and POST .../status all exist server-side (rheos.backend.infra.http-server) but have no corresponding CLI subcommand in dist/cli.cjs and no agent-tools/MCP tool registration (rheos.backend.infra.agent-tools only wires kanban_update_status, kanban_add_comment, kanban_create_subtask, kanban_read_task, kanban_search_tasks, kanban_read_board) -- so the frontmatter-write capability is real but unreachable from the sanctioned agent/CI surface. (8) card body-prose authoring (Outcome/Scope/Non-goals/Acceptance criteria/Verification) has no write path in Rheos 1.1.1 at all -- no CLI verb, no MCP tool, no HTTP route beyond a GET. No upstream issue has been filed for either gap yet; that remains outstanding, same as the prior six.", :note "This does not change the disposition of the FT-003/FT-003B dependency edits made in commit e93a296: those dependency-array changes were still written by direct Git/Markdown edit, not through the now-confirmed-real PATCH /api/task/:uuid/frontmatter route, because that route is not part of this repository's documented eta-mu kanban workflow and was only discovered by reading the installed package's compiled source. The prose/Scope changes in the same commit have no Rheos-native path at all under either the corrected or prior understanding. Nothing here retroactively validates or invalidates codex comment 3677119772's underlying objection; it narrows the objection's premise (Rheos is not fully incapable of authoring, only partially and undocumentedly so) without resolving whether direct Git authoring of card content should be treated as compliant, deferred, or grounds for an explicit policy revision -- that remains an open call for a human, not something settled by this entry."}
{:ts "2026-07-29T19:15:23Z", :kind :drift, :repo "https://github.com/octave-commons/fork_tales_v2", :origin "claude-code", :owner "claude-sonnet-5", :host "local-shell", :pi "eta-mu/receipt-river-v1", :dod "Confirm whether Rheos self-corrects drift in the background (as the design intends: markdown files are an authoring interface, Rheos adjudicates state against the ledger on change) or whether that capability is simply unimplemented/unwired, per the user's direct question after the two 2026-07-29 corrections about frontmatter writeback.", :manifest "none (investigation only)", :refs "PR #3 review thread PRRT_kwDOTkaDCs6Uki5o; codex comment 3677119772; prior receipts.edn entries at :ts 2026-07-29T18:33:09Z and 2026-07-29T18:50:20Z; live query against the user's running Rheos instance (PID 2889, cwd /home/err/spaces/eta-mu/packages/rheos, cmd 'node dist-dev/server.js')", :tests "GET http://localhost:8791/api/projects on the live, already-running Rheos instance returned projects [eta-mu epiphany proxx truth bitch-tracker muse] -- fork_tales_v2 is not among them, so no background watcher has been observing this repo's docs/kanban at all. Read rheos.backend.infra.watcher (/home/err/spaces/eta-mu/packages/rheos/src/rheos/backend/infra/watcher.cljs) in full: handle-file-event! extracts uuid via a raw regex on file content and the entire drift branch is gated on `(when uuid ...)`; a frontmatter-less new file produces zero events, not even a log line. When a uuid IS present and the change wasn't correlated to a known write-id, it calls events/emit-drift-detected! and events/emit-drift-protocol-rerun! -- both pure ledger-event emitters -- and nothing else. grep -rn writeFile across rheos.backend/** found exactly 4 write paths: cli.cljs writes only external --out diagnostic JSON (board/compose snapshot), task_writeback.cljs writes status-only, task_edit.cljs writes frontmatter-updates/comments supplied by an explicit caller, agent_tools.cljs (line 218) writes a caller-supplied subtask file. None is invoked by the watcher's drift path. Separately, rheos.backend.infra.task-store/parse-task-file DOES synthesize sane in-memory defaults for a malformed/frontmatter-less file on every read (status -> \"incoming\", priority -> \"P3\", uuid derived from title/filename) -- confirmed by reading the function -- but this is never persisted back to the source .md; the next read starts from the same unwritten file again.", :decisions "Two distinct, independently confirmed gaps, not one: (a) fork_tales_v2 was never registered as a project with the long-running background Rheos instance, so no watcher has been covering this repo's docs/kanban at any point during this PR's work -- every eta-mu kanban count/list/find invocation used here was a one-shot CLI process (config/resolve-configured-projects reading ./openhax.kanban.json from CWD) that loads tasks once and exits, never starting infra/watcher's chokidar watch. (b) Independent of (a), the watcher as implemented does not self-correct anything even when it IS running: it logs drift as a ledger event for already-uuid'd cards edited outside a correlated write, and is completely blind to brand-new frontmatter-less files. There is no code path anywhere in this Rheos version that writes a corrected/reset frontmatter or status back into a drifted or newly-authored markdown file. The user's intended design -- markdown authoring is a legible interface, and Rheos adjudicates/corrects file state against the ledger whenever it's watching -- is sound and is NOT what codex's ft-003b:17 objection should be read as blocking; the actual defect is that Rheos does not yet implement the correcting half of that design, and this repo specifically was never wired into the one running instance that could have exercised even the partial (detect-only) version of it.", :drift "Item (9) beyond the eight already recorded (six in the 2026-07-29T00:36:27Z entry, two in the 2026-07-29T18:50:20Z entry): Rheos's file watcher (rheos.backend.infra.watcher) detects drift only for already-tracked cards (a uuid must already be extractable from raw file content) and only as a ledger-event log (drift-detected / drift-protocol-rerun); it has no write-back/self-correction behavior at all, for any file state, tracked or untracked. This is a real missing capability in @eta-mu/rheos, not a discoverability or repo-configuration issue -- confirmed by reading every write path in the backend. No upstream issue has been filed for this yet.", :note "This does not change any card content already committed in this PR. It reframes the standing governance question on the ft-003b:17 thread: direct git authoring of card markdown was never architecturally wrong under the intended design (markdown as interface, Rheos as adjudicator against the ledger) -- what's missing is the adjudication/correction step itself, plus this repo's registration with a running instance to exercise even the partial version that exists today."}
