{:ts "2026-07-29T19:22:39Z", :kind :ops, :repo "https://github.com/octave-commons/fork_tales_v2", :origin "claude-code", :owner "claude-sonnet-5", :host "local-shell", :pi "eta-mu/receipt-river-v1", :dod "Register fork_tales_v2 with the user's persistent rheos.service systemd --user unit so the live background Rheos instance actually watches docs/kanban here going forward, closing the (2026-07-29T19:15:23Z) 'this repo isn't registered anywhere' half of the drift-detection gap.", :manifest "/home/err/spaces/eta-mu/kanban/openhax.kanban.json (outside this repo -- the multi-project config consumed by ~/.config/systemd/user/rheos.service)", :refs "systemd --user unit rheos.service (WorkingDirectory /home/err/spaces/eta-mu/packages/rheos, KANBAN_CONFIG=../../kanban/openhax.kanban.json); prior receipts.edn entries at :ts 2026-07-29T19:15:23Z and 2026-07-29T19:19:34Z", :tests "Added a `fork-tales-v2` entry to the projects array in /home/err/spaces/eta-mu/kanban/openhax.kanban.json: {tasksDir ../../fork_tales_v2/docs/kanban, fsm {extends promethean, buildGateCommands [clojure -M:test], cwd ../../fork_tales_v2}} -- the same extends/buildGateCommands/cwd shape already used by the existing `epiphany` entry in the same file, confirming that pattern is the house convention, not something invented for this PR. Validated the edited JSON parses (python3 json.load). `systemctl --user restart rheos.service` succeeded; `systemctl --user status` shows active/running under the same PID pattern. `journalctl --user -u rheos.service -n 30` shows `Watcher started for fork-tales-v2 : /home/err/spaces/fork_tales_v2/docs/kanban` alongside the six prior projects (no error lines). `GET http://localhost:8791/api/projects` now lists `fork-tales-v2` among seven projects. `GET http://localhost:8791/api/board?project=fork-tales-v2` returns totalTasks 27 with per-column counts matching `eta-mu kanban count` exactly (icebox 6, incoming 11 [visible per-card in the columns payload], breakdown 4, ready 2,